\par \pard\fi0\li0\qj\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -189\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) [\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 Text\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 :] >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Incipit de uoce.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 < >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 P\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 <{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 HYLOSOPHI diffiniunt, uocem esse aerem tenuissimum ictum}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  uel suum sensibile aurium, id est quod proprie auribus accidit. ...\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  - \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ...\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (189\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ...\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [getilgte Stelle, kein Textverlust] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Alie pene omnes indifferenter et preponi et subponi possunt, ut et, atque, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [Zusatz, in der Ed. nicht erfasst: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 pene dicit pronomen,\plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24  qu\u281 \'ea semper supponitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ]\plain \f2\i\lang1024\fs24 , qu\u281 \'ea poetice postponuntur, alias au\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 tem non, vt Uirgilius in viiii: ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ...\plain \f3\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nam neque erant astrorum ignes nec lucidius ether \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [Ed.: aethra]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  siderea polus. EXPLICIT LIBER III PRISCIANI. Deo gracias cvm amen fiat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
